      "source": [
        "#### Hyperparameter Tuning\n",
        "\n",
        "The neural network was tuned systematically by changing one hyperparameter at a time while keeping the same training and validation sets.\n",
        "\n",
        "The experiments tested different learning rates, network sizes, dropout rates, and batch sizes.\n",
        "\n",
        "The results showed that three experiments achieved the highest validation accuracy of **88%**: a learning rate of **0.01**, a larger network, and higher dropout.\n",
        "\n",
        "Among these experiments, the **Higher Dropout** configuration achieved the lowest validation loss of **0.3188**, while also achieving **88% validation accuracy**. Therefore, it was selected as the best configuration based on validation performance.\n",
        "\n",
        "The results also showed that a very low learning rate of **0.0001** performed worse, with a validation loss of **0.3745**. Changing the batch size to 16 did not provide a significant improvement.\n",
        "\n",
        "Overall, increasing the dropout rate provided the best balance between validation loss and validation accuracy among the tested configurations.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "F-UdapaaqXb4"
      }
