      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#### Why This Architecture\n",
        "\n",
        "The network is intentionally simple, mirroring the single-neuron math\n",
        "covered earlier: each `Dense` layer is a set of neurons, each computing a\n",
        "weighted sum plus bias (`dot(features, weights) + bias`), then passing it\n",
        "through an activation function. Two hidden layers (32 → 16 neurons) with\n",
        "`relu` activations let the network learn non-linear combinations of\n",
        "features that Logistic Regression's single linear boundary can't capture.\n",
        "`Dropout` randomly disables a fraction of neurons during training — a\n",
        "regularization technique preventing the network from overfitting to the\n",
        "training data, similar in spirit to Ridge/Lasso shrinking weights. The\n",
        "final layer uses `sigmoid` to output a probability between 0 and 1,\n",
        "exactly like Logistic Regression's output, making the two models directly\n",
        "comparable."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "HciW9MZHb0ig"
      }
    },
